insert into public.document_translations (document_id, lang, card_json, presentation_json, key_points, a_verifier, source_publication_date, content_sha256, fr_a_jour)
select d.id, 'en', $mgjson${"badge":"SFAR/FCVD/SFCD/SFED/SFM/SFR/SPILF/SFPT — RFE, validated 24/06/2026","title":"Intra-abdominal infections in adults — management","short":"SFAR, in association with FCVD/SFCD/SFED/SFM/SFR/SPILF/SFPT, \"Therapeutic management of intra-abdominal infections in adults\" (\"Prise en charge thérapeutique des Infections intra-abdominales de l'adulte\"), RFE (formalized expert recommendations), validated by the SFAR Clinical Guidelines Committee (09/06/2026) and the SFAR Board of Directors (24/06/2026) — very recent document found through a web search (absent from this site's usual index at the date of its publication). CLINICALLY UPDATES the fiche \"Management of intra-abdominal infections\" (SFAR/SFCD/SPILF/AFC consensus conference, 2014/2015), kept on this site for its historical value. Scope: adults requiring interventional management (surgery, endoscopy or interventional radiology). Covers 3 fields: initial management (source control, empirical antibiotic therapy detailed by community-acquired/healthcare-associated setting with ESBL/MDR risk factors, referral to critical care); clinical monitoring and treatment duration (de-escalation, antibiotic/antifungal durations according to the setting); evolving complications (reoperation, antibiotic therapy of a postoperative complication). 43 recommendations (GRADE 1: 8, GRADE 2: 13, expert opinion: 21, no recommendation: 1) — count verified as exactly identical to the one announced by the source document itself in its \"Summary of results\" section, no discrepancy.","society":"SFAR / FCVD / SFCD / SFED / SFM / SFR / SPILF / SFPT","version":"2026","validated":"SFAR Clinical Guidelines Committee (09/06/2026) and SFAR Board of Directors (24/06/2026)","methodology":"GRADE grid — GRADE 1/2 (strong/weak, for or against), AE (expert opinion), no recommendation (chip \"0/\") — 43 recommendations (GRADE 1: 8, GRADE 2: 13, AE: 21, 0/: 1), count identical to the one announced by the source"}$mgjson$::jsonb, $mgjson${"v":1,"key":"infections_intra_abdominales_2026","lang":"en","chip_legend":{"1+/1-":"strong recommendation, for / against (GRADE)","2+/2-":"weak recommendation, for / against (GRADE)","AE":"expert opinion (avis d'experts) — label kept as in the French source","0/":"no recommendation (absence de recommandation)","RÉGL":"regulatory reminder, not a GRADE grade (rappel réglementaire)"},"sections":[{"title":"Intra-abdominal infections in adults — Fields 1 to 3","items":[{"t":"panel","tone":"default","content":{"t":"p","html":"<b>Very recent document</b> (validated by the SFAR Board on 24/06/2026) — found through a web search (absent from <code>library_final.json</code> at the time of publication). <b>UPDATES</b> the fiche \"Management of intra-abdominal infections\" (SFAR/SFCD/SPILF/AFC consensus conference, 2014/2015, kept for its historical value). <b>Scope:</b> adults requiring interventional management (surgery, endoscopy, interventional radiology) — excludes pediatrics, aplasia/organ transplantation, cirrhosis, isolated biliary/hepatic infections, non-operated appendicitis.","style":"body"}},{"t":"table","rows":[[{"t":"chip","label":"1+"},{"t":"chip","label":"1-"},{"t":"chip","label":"2+"},{"t":"chip","label":"2-"},{"t":"chip","label":"AE"},{"t":"chip","label":"0/"},{"t":"p","html":"<b>GRADE grid</b> — <b>1+/1-</b>: strong recommendation, for/against; <b>2+/2-</b>: weak recommendation, for/against; <b>AE</b>: expert opinion (always strong agreement); <b>0/</b>: no recommendation (insufficient literature). Count announced by the source itself — 43 recommendations (GRADE 1: 8, GRADE 2: 13, AE: 21, no recommendation: 1) — verified exact by a complete recount of the summary table, no discrepancy.","style":"badge_head"}]]},{"t":"section","text":"Field 1 — Initial management: source control","color":"navy"},{"t":"table","rows":[[{"t":"p","html":"Ref.","style":"head_w"},{"t":"p","html":"Recommendation","style":"head_w"},{"t":"p","html":"Grade","style":"head_w_c"}],[{"t":"p","html":"1.1.1","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Hemodynamic instability: surgical source control of the infection as quickly as possible, combined with lavage of the entire abdominal cavity.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"1+"}],[{"t":"p","html":"1.1.2","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Hemodynamic instability not/poorly controlled intraoperatively: the experts suggest \"Damage Control\" surgery or \"abbreviated laparotomy\", with definitive reoperation at 24-48h after stabilization.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"AE"}],[{"t":"p","html":"1.1.3","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Suspected peritonitis from hollow-viscus perforation: discuss the surgical approach (laparoscopy or laparotomy) between surgeon and anesthesiologist-intensivist — laparoscopy possible if there is no persistent hypotension and the lesion is accessible according to the surgeon's expertise.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"AE"}],[{"t":"p","html":"1.1.4","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Stable patient, postoperative infection with an accessible collection: minimally invasive treatment as first-line (interventional endoscopy or imaging-guided percutaneous drainage), notably in case of secondary fistula.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"2+"}],[{"t":"p","html":"1.1.5","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Perforated purulent sigmoid diverticulitis (Hinchey III) without sepsis: do not perform peritoneal lavage alone without resection — perform sigmoid resection with primary anastomosis (protected or not by ileostomy) combined with peritoneal lavage.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"1+"}]]},{"t":"section","text":"Field 1 — Initial empirical antibiotic therapy","color":"navy"},{"t":"table","rows":[[{"t":"p","html":"Ref.","style":"head_w"},{"t":"p","html":"Recommendation","style":"head_w"},{"t":"p","html":"Grade","style":"head_w_c"}],[{"t":"p","html":"1.2.1","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Community-acquired without sepsis/shock: 3rd-generation cephalosporin (cefotaxime, ceftriaxone) + metronidazole.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"2+"}],[{"t":"p","html":"1.2.2","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Community-acquired without sepsis/shock: do not take ESBL-producing Enterobacterales into account in the empirical choice.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"2-"}],[{"t":"p","html":"1.2.3","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Community-acquired, patient in sepsis: carbapenem to be considered only if there is a documented history of ESBL colonization/infection < 6 months.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"AE"}],[{"t":"p","html":"1.2.4","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Community-acquired, septic shock, without ESBL risk factor: piperacillin-tazobactam.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"2+"}],[{"t":"p","html":"1.2.5","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Community-acquired, septic shock, ≥1 ESBL risk factor: carbapenem according to local prevalence.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"2+"}],[{"t":"p","html":"1.2.6","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Healthcare-associated (1st episode), without MDR risk factor, including sepsis/shock: cefepime + metronidazole.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"1+"}],[{"t":"p","html":"1.2.7","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Same setting, if plasma monitoring of cefepime is not possible: piperacillin-tazobactam according to local ecology.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"AE"}],[{"t":"p","html":"1.2.8","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Healthcare-associated, septic shock, cefepime + metronidazole (not active on enterococci): add linezolid, vancomycin or teicoplanin.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"AE"}],[{"t":"p","html":"1.2.9","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Healthcare-associated, piperacillin-tazobactam chosen + risk factor for ampicillin-resistant enterococcus: add linezolid, vancomycin or teicoplanin.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"AE"}],[{"t":"p","html":"1.2.10","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"1st healthcare-associated episode, ≥2 MDR criteria (table below): carbapenem from the outset — a single criterion is sufficient if sepsis/septic shock.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"1+"}],[{"t":"p","html":"1.2.11","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Community-acquired (± sepsis/shock), β-lactam allergy excluding cephalosporins and carbapenems: levofloxacin + metronidazole, or moxifloxacin* (*corrected QT checked); or tigecycline/eravacycline if fluoroquinolones are contraindicated, reassessment at 48h.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"AE"}],[{"t":"p","html":"1.2.12","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Healthcare-associated, same allergy context: ciprofloxacin + metronidazole (± linezolid/vancomycin/teicoplanin); or aztreonam + metronidazole (± same); or tigecycline/eravacycline + ciprofloxacin.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"AE"}],[{"t":"p","html":"1.2.13","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Community-acquired with sepsis/shock or healthcare-associated: antifungal treatment if direct examination is positive for yeasts, or ≥3 criteria among hemodynamic failure, female sex, supramesocolic surgery, antibiotic therapy > 48h.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"2+"}]]},{"t":"table","rows":[[{"t":"p","html":"<b>Bacterium</b>","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"<b>Risk factors retained</b>","style":"cell_b"}],[{"t":"p","html":"ESBL","style":"cell"},{"t":"p","html":"History of ESBL infection/colonization < 6 months; high local prevalence; amoxicillin-clavulanic acid/2nd-generation cephalosporins/3rd-generation cephalosporins/fluoroquinolones within 6 months; travel to an endemic area < 3 months; living in a medico-social institution with a permanent invasive device (indwelling urinary catheter and/or gastrostomy).","style":"cell"}],[{"t":"p","html":"MDR (in the broad sense)","style":"cell"},{"t":"p","html":"3rd-generation cephalosporins or fluoroquinolones within 3 months; documented carriage < 3 months of ESBL or ceftazidime-resistant P. aeruginosa; hospitalization abroad < 12 months; living in a medico-social institution with a permanent invasive device; failure of a previous treatment with 3rd-generation cephalosporins/fluoroquinolones/piperacillin-tazobactam; recurrence < 15 days of an infection treated ≥ 3 days with piperacillin-tazobactam.","style":"cell"}],[{"t":"p","html":"Ampicillin-resistant enterococcus","style":"cell"},{"t":"p","html":"Suspected peritonitis of hepatobiliary origin; history of liver transplantation, immunocompromised patient; patient already on antibiotic therapy or prior antibiotic therapy with a cephalosporin.","style":"cell"}]]},{"t":"p","html":"Table 1 of the source — risk factors for resistant bacteria, attached to R1.2.3/1.2.5/1.2.10.","style":"source"},{"t":"section","text":"Field 1 — Referral to critical care","color":"navy"},{"t":"table","rows":[[{"t":"p","html":"Ref.","style":"head_w"},{"t":"p","html":"Recommendation","style":"head_w"},{"t":"p","html":"Grade","style":"head_w_c"}],[{"t":"p","html":"1.3.1","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Septic shock or sepsis: systematic admission to critical care.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"1+"}],[{"t":"p","html":"1.3.2","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Without shock or sepsis: base the admission decision on age > 60 years, comorbidities, generalized peritonitis.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"2+"}],[{"t":"p","html":"1.3.3","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Without shock or sepsis: the CPIRO, WSES Sepsis Severity Score or PIPAS Severity Score scores may be used to identify patients requiring admission to critical care.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"AE"}]]},{"t":"section","text":"Field 2 — Clinical monitoring & treatment duration","color":"navy"},{"t":"table","rows":[[{"t":"p","html":"Ref.","style":"head_w"},{"t":"p","html":"Recommendation","style":"head_w"},{"t":"p","html":"Grade","style":"head_w_c"}],[{"t":"p","html":"2.1.1","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"First 5 postoperative days: do not systematically perform — PCT/CRP measurement, systematic repeat laparotomy (except initial Damage Control or doubt about bowel viability), microbiological cultures of drainage fluid.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"2-"}],[{"t":"p","html":"2.1.2","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Favorable course: the experts suggest not performing systematic abdominal computed tomography in the first 5 days.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"AE"}],[{"t":"p","html":"2.2.1","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Uncomplicated acute appendicitis, source control achieved: no postoperative antibiotic therapy beyond intraoperative antibiotic prophylaxis (single dose).","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"1-"}],[{"t":"p","html":"2.2.2","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Complicated acute appendicitis, source control achieved: short postoperative empirical antibiotic therapy (2 days).","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"1+"}],[{"t":"p","html":"2.2.3","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Complicated community-acquired infection (other than appendicitis), source control achieved: limit the duration of antibiotic therapy to 4 days, including in case of initial sepsis or control by percutaneous/endoscopic drainage.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"1+"}],[{"t":"p","html":"2.2.4","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Healthcare-associated (other than postoperative), without sepsis/shock, source control achieved: the experts suggest limiting the duration to 4 days.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"AE"}],[{"t":"p","html":"2.2.5","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Healthcare-associated, sepsis/shock, source control achieved: limit the duration of antibiotic therapy to 8 days.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"2+"}],[{"t":"p","html":"2.3.1","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Antifungal started from the outset, culture positive for Candida sp.: the experts suggest limiting treatment to 8 days if source control is rapid/effective, the course is favorable, and there is no candidemia — all criteria met.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"AE"}],[{"t":"p","html":"2.3.1bis","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Same circumstances but the criteria above not all met: no recommendation on the necessary duration of antifungal treatment.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"0/"}],[{"t":"p","html":"2.3.2","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Antifungal started from the outset, Candida culture negative or not available: measure β-D-glucan at D0 and D3; early discontinuation may be considered if both samples are negative.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"AE"}],[{"t":"p","html":"2.4.1","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Favorable course after source control: de-escalate antibiotic therapy after the bacteriological results.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"2+"}],[{"t":"p","html":"2.4.2","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Favorable course after source control: antifungal de-escalation may be considered if the patient is not neutropenic, source control is adequate, initial samples are interpretable, there is clinical improvement at 48-72h, initial treatment is optimized (PK/PD), and post-de-escalation duration is > 24h.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"AE"}]]},{"t":"section","text":"Field 3 — Evolving complications","color":"navy"},{"t":"table","rows":[[{"t":"p","html":"Ref.","style":"head_w"},{"t":"p","html":"Recommendation","style":"head_w"},{"t":"p","html":"Grade","style":"head_w_c"}],[{"t":"p","html":"3.1.1","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Unfavorable course, suspected infectious complication: urgent source control.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"2+"}],[{"t":"p","html":"3.1.2","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Hemodynamically stable patient, unfavorable course: the experts suggest a minimally invasive approach (percutaneous and/or endoscopic) if technically possible.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"AE"}],[{"t":"p","html":"3.2.1","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Early phase (≤72h), fever or ileus or persistent organ failure: suspect an infectious complication or imperfect source control, perform urgent source control.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"2+"}],[{"t":"p","html":"3.2.2","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Early phase (≤72h), unfavorable course: CT scan resulting from a multidisciplinary discussion, not systematic; do not measure CRP/PCT; do not culture fluid from a drain already in place.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"AE"}],[{"t":"p","html":"3.2.3","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Late phase (>72h), unfavorable course: contrast-enhanced thoraco-abdomino-pelvic CT scan (± intraluminal opacification if gastric/colonic procedure).","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"AE"}],[{"t":"p","html":"3.3.1","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Postoperative complication: empirical antibiotic therapy covering microorganisms at risk of resistance (multidrug-resistant Enterobacterales including ESBL, P. aeruginosa, E. faecium), adapted to local and patient ecology.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"2+"}],[{"t":"p","html":"3.3.2","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Postoperative complication: the experts suggest secondarily adjusting antibiotic therapy to intraoperative/reoperation samples, or to blood cultures alone if samples are non-contributory.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"AE"}],[{"t":"p","html":"3.3.3","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Critical care or risk of overdose: therapeutic drug monitoring for optimized dose adjustment (β-lactams: SFAR/SFPT 2018 recommendations).","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"AE"}],[{"t":"p","html":"3.3.4","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Source control achieved, clinical improvement on appropriate antibiotic therapy: limit the duration to 8 days — beyond that, multidisciplinary discussion (anesthesiologist-intensivists, surgeons, infectious disease specialists, microbiologists).","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"AE"}],[{"t":"p","html":"3.3.5","style":"cell_b"},{"t":"p","html":"Poor course on antibiotic therapy with signs of hemodynamic severity, or yeasts on direct examination: systematic empirical antifungal treatment, echinocandins preferred.","style":"cell"},{"t":"chip","label":"AE"}]]},{"t":"section","text":"Sources and disclaimer","color":"grey"},{"t":"p","html":"<b>Source document:</b> SFAR/FCVD/SFCD/SFED/SFM/SFR/SPILF/SFPT, \"Therapeutic management of intra-abdominal infections in adults\" (\"Prise en charge thérapeutique des Infections intra-abdominales de l'adulte\"), RFE, validated by the SFAR Clinical Guidelines Committee (09/06/2026) and the SFAR Board of Directors (24/06/2026).","style":"source"},{"t":"p","html":"<b>Source URL:</b> https://sfar.org/prise-en-charge-therapeutique-des-infections-intra-abdominales-de-ladulte/","style":"source"},{"t":"p","html":"<b>Coverage:</b> the 43 recommendations of the document (Fields 1 to 3) are reproduced in full (GRADE 1: 8, GRADE 2: 13, expert opinion: 21, no recommendation: 1) — count identical to the one announced by the source itself in its \"Summary of results\" section, verified by exhaustive recount of the summary table. Clinically updates/supersedes the fiche \"Management of intra-abdominal infections\" (SFAR/SFCD/SPILF/AFC consensus conference, 2014/2015, kept on this site for its historical value). Detailed scientific rationale (studies, meta-analyses, same document, 91 pages) not included.","style":"source"},{"t":"panel","tone":"grey","content":{"t":"p","html":"<b>Disclaimer:</b> this fiche is an independent summary of the 43 recommendations of this reference document. It does not replace the full text or the scientific rationale. This fiche is neither published nor validated by the SFAR or the co-signatory societies.","style":"body_sm"}}]}]}$mgjson$::jsonb, $mgjson$[{"ref":"1.1.1","grade":"1+","fr":"Instabilité hémodynamique : contrôle de la source infectieuse par voie chirurgicale le plus rapidement possible, associé à un lavage de l'ensemble de la cavité abdominale.","en":"Hemodynamic instability: surgical source control of the infection as quickly as possible, combined with lavage of the entire abdominal cavity."},{"ref":"1.2.10","grade":"1+","fr":"1er épisode associé aux soins, ≥2 critères de BMR (tableau ci-dessous) : carbapénème d'emblée — un seul critère suffit si sepsis/choc septique.","en":"1st healthcare-associated episode, ≥2 MDR criteria (table below): carbapenem from the outset — a single criterion is sufficient if sepsis/septic shock."},{"ref":"1.3.1","grade":"1+","fr":"Choc septique ou sepsis : admission systématique en soins critiques.","en":"Septic shock or sepsis: systematic admission to critical care."},{"ref":"2.2.1","grade":"1-","fr":"Appendicite aiguë non compliquée, contrôle de la source obtenu : pas d'antibiothérapie postopératoire au-delà de l'antibioprophylaxie peropératoire (dose unique).","en":"Uncomplicated acute appendicitis, source control achieved: no postoperative antibiotic therapy beyond intraoperative antibiotic prophylaxis (single dose)."},{"ref":"2.2.3","grade":"1+","fr":"Infection communautaire compliquée (hors appendicite), contrôle de la source obtenu : limiter la durée d'antibiothérapie à 4 jours, y compris en cas de sepsis initial ou de contrôle par drainage percutané/endoscopique.","en":"Complicated community-acquired infection (other than appendicitis), source control achieved: limit the duration of antibiotic therapy to 4 days, including in case of initial sepsis or control by percutaneous/endoscopic drainage."}]$mgjson$::jsonb, $mgjson$["À VÉRIFIER : date de publication retenue = 24/06/2026 (validation par le CA de la SFAR, seule date de mise en ligne présente dans la bibliothèque) ; le CRC l'avait validé le 09/06/2026. Confirmer la date de mise en ligne effective sur sfar.org.","À VÉRIFIER : l'identifiant « 2.3.1bis » (ligne « absence de recommandation » sur la durée du traitement antifongique lorsque les critères de 2.3.1 ne sont pas tous réunis) est un identifiant de l'atelier ; confirmer avec la source s'il s'agit d'une recommandation distincte ou du second volet de R2.3.1 (le décompte 43 = 8 + 13 + 21 + 1 concorde exactement avec la source).","À VÉRIFIER : la ligne 1.1.5 (diverticulite sigmoïdienne Hinchey III) regroupe un « ne pas faire » (lavage seul sans résection) et un « faire » (résection avec anastomose primaire) sous la puce « 1+ » ; le signe est celui imprimé par la source (« Grade 1+ »), mais le relecteur doit confirmer qu'il s'agit bien d'une seule recommandation.","À VÉRIFIER (contrôle positif) : contrairement aux autres fiches 2026, la source imprime ici les signes (« Grade 1+ », « Grade 2– », 36 occurrences signées dans le texte extrait) ; les puces 1+/1-/2+/2- de cette fiche sont donc celles de la source, non déduites. Ce contrôle a été fait par recherche de motif dans sources/infections_intra_abdominales.txt, pas ligne à ligne : à confirmer lors de la relecture médicale.","À VÉRIFIER : notes internes de l'atelier (« trouvé via recherche web », « absent de library_final.json », « supersede ») dans l'introduction, la couverture et la méta ; traduites telles quelles, à retirer avant publication.","À VÉRIFIER : sigles traduits — BLSE → ESBL, BMR → MDR (bactéries multirésistantes), C3G → 3rd-generation cephalosporins, ATCD → history ; « B-D-glucane » (source française) rendu « β-D-glucan » ; « cœlioscopie » → laparoscopy ; « laparotomie écourtée » → abbreviated laparotomy ; scores CPIRO / WSES / PIPAS conservés.","À VÉRIFIER (droits) : le tableau 1 (facteurs de risque de bactéries résistantes) reprend un tableau de la source (CDC §12.4 : pas de reproduction à l'identique) — statut juridique à valider."]$mgjson$::jsonb, '2026-06-24', '28b95956280b33df3e62ed5a8014eb9cf6d453aaf52feb9c62b32f4ae515b706', true
from public.documents d where d.fiche_key = 'infections_intra_abdominales_2026'
